<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Kinematics: stationary times, direction and acceleration (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A particle moves along a straight line. Its position, in metres, after \( t \) seconds is</p>
\[ s(t) = {@st@}, \qquad t \ge 0. \]
<p>(a) Find the velocity \( v(t) \) and the acceleration \( a(t) \).</p>
<div>\( v(t) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div>\( a(t) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(b) At what times is the particle stationary? Enter a set, e.g. <code>{2, 7}</code>.</p>
<div>\( t \in \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>(c) The particle moves in the <strong>negative</strong> direction for</p>
<div>[[input:ans4]] \( < t < \) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans4]] [[validation:ans5]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt4]]</div>
<p>(d) Find the acceleration at the first stationary time.</p>
<div>Acceleration \( = \) [[input:ans6]] m/s\(^2\) [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt5]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> Differentiate once for velocity and again for acceleration:</p>
\[ v(t) = s'(t) = {@vt@} = {@factor(vt)@}, \qquad a(t) = v'(t) = {@acc@}. \]
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Stationary means \( v(t) = 0 \): \( {@factor(vt)@} = 0 \), so \( t = {@pp@} \) s or \( t = {@qp@} \) s.</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> \( v(t) \) is a quadratic with a positive leading coefficient, so it is negative <em>between</em> its roots. Test a value: at \( t = {@(pp+qp)/2@} \), \( v = {@subst((pp+qp)/2, t, vt)@} < 0 \). The particle moves in the negative direction for \( {@pp@} < t < {@qp@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(d)</strong> \( a({@pp@}) = {@acc@} \big|_{t={@pp@}} = {@apq@} \) m/s\(^2\). The particle is momentarily at rest and the negative acceleration is turning it round to move in the negative direction.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>5</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[/* v(t) = 3 (t - pp)(t - qp) with 0 < pp < qp and pp + qp even, so that
   s(t) = t^3 - 3(pp+qp)/2 t^2 + 3 pp qp t + s0 has integer coefficients. */
pp  : rand([1, 2, 3, 4]);
qp  : pp + rand([2, 4]);
s0  : rand_with_prohib(-5, 5, [0]);
st  : t^3 - 3*(pp + qp)/2*t^2 + 3*pp*qp*t + s0;
vt  : expand(diff(st, t));
acc : diff(vt, t);
ta3 : {pp, qp};
apq : subst(pp, t, acc);                  /* acceleration at the first stationary time */
w_mid : {(pp + qp)/2};                   /* solved a(t) = 0 instead */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
